{"name":"Yellow Bell Pepper","hex":"#ffdd33","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"yellow","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of sunflower petals and lemons; the color obtained by mixing green and red light, or by subtracting blue from white light; the color evoked by light of wavelength around 580 nm; one of the three primary colors in subtractive color systems.","The middle light in a set of three traffic lights, the lighting of which indicates that drivers should stop short of the intersection if it is safe to do so."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a yellow hue.","Lacking courage."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/yellow"},{"term":"bell","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A percussive instrument made of metal or other hard material, typically but not always in the shape of an inverted cup with a flared rim, which resonates when struck.","An instrument that emits a ringing sound, situated on a bicycle's handlebar and used by the cyclist to warn of their presence."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To attach a bell to.","To shape so that it flares out like a bell."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bell"},{"term":"pepper","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A plant of the family Piperaceae.","A spice prepared from the fermented, dried, unripe berries of this plant."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To add pepper to.","To strike with something made up of small particles."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pepper"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bell pepper","blocks":[{"text":"The bell pepper is the fruit of plants in the Grossum Group of the species Capsicum annuum. Cultivars of the plant produce fruits in different colors, including red, yellow, orange, green, white, and purple. Bell peppers are sometimes grouped with less pungent chili varieties as \"sweet peppers\". While they are botanically fruits—classified as berries—they are commonly used as a vegetable ingredient or side dish. Other varieties of the genus Capsicum are categorized as chili peppers when they are cultivated for their pungency, including some varieties of Capsicum annuum."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/Green-Yellow-Red-Pepper-2009.jpg/330px-Green-Yellow-Red-Pepper-2009.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bell_pepper"},{"title":"Yellow bell","blocks":[{"text":"Yellow bell is a common name for several plants with yellow flowers and may refer to:"},{"items":["Allamanda, genus of flowering plants in the dogbane family","Fritillaria pudica, species of flowering sagebrush","Tecoma stans, species of flowering perennial shrub in the trumpet vine family"]}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yellow_bell"},{"title":"Bell","blocks":[{"text":"A bell is a directly struck idiophone percussion instrument. Most bells have the shape of a hollow cup that—when struck—vibrates in a single strong strike tone, with its sides forming an efficient resonator. The strike may be made by an internal \"clapper\" or \"uvula\", an external hammer, or—in small bells—by a small loose sphere enclosed within the body of the bell."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Parts_of_a_Bell.svg/330px-Parts_of_a_Bell.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bell"},{"title":"Yellow","blocks":[{"text":"Yellow is a color between green and orange on the spectrum of light. It is evoked by light with a dominant wavelength of roughly 575–585 nm. It is a primary color in subtractive color systems, used in painting or color printing. In the RGB color model, used to create colors on television and computer screens, yellow is a secondary color made by combining red and green at equal intensity. Carotenoids give the characteristic yellow color to autumn leaves, corn, canaries, daffodils, and lemons, as well as egg yolks, buttercups, and bananas. They absorb light energy and protect plants from photo damage in some cases. Sunlight has a slight yellowish hue when the Sun is near the horizon, due to atmospheric scattering of shorter wavelengths."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Cornwall_Daffodils.jpg/330px-Cornwall_Daffodils.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yellow"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/Colorful_Bell_Peppers.JPG/500px-Colorful_Bell_Peppers.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/Colorful_Bell_Peppers.JPG/1280px-Colorful_Bell_Peppers.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/Colorful_Bell_Peppers.JPG/500px-Colorful_Bell_Peppers.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A variety of colored bell peppers","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AColorful_Bell_Peppers.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/November_15%2C_2012%2C_The_Right_Cut_%288223639251%29.jpg/500px-November_15%2C_2012%2C_The_Right_Cut_%288223639251%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/November_15%2C_2012%2C_The_Right_Cut_%288223639251%29.jpg/500px-November_15%2C_2012%2C_The_Right_Cut_%288223639251%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Chef chopping bell peppers","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANovember_15%2C_2012%2C_The_Right_Cut_(8223639251).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/13th-12th_Cent._BC_Shang_Bronze_Bell.jpg/500px-13th-12th_Cent._BC_Sha